  "mainEntity": {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Do Interior Log Walls Really Need a Sealer?",
    "text": "Do Interior Log Walls Really Need a Sealer?",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You might be wondering if your interior log walls actually need a clear coat or sealer. It's a common question, and the short answer is often yes! While exterior logs face harsh weather, interior logs still benefit greatly from protection. Think of a clear coat or sealer as a shield for your beautiful wood. It helps protect the logs from daily wear and tear, dust, and even accidental spills, making them easier to clean and maintain. Products designed for interior log surfaces are chosen to protect logs and prevent deterioration, which means your logs will stay looking great for longer. Unlike exterior sealers that need to be super tough against the elements, interior sealers can focus more on enhancing the natural beauty of the wood while providing that protective layer. The good news is that many interior log finishes are formulated to be breathable, which means they protect the wood without trapping moisture, allowing the logs to 'breathe' naturally. If you're unsure about the best system for your specific logs, HH Remodeling LLC can help you figure out the ideal solution.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
      }
    }
  },
